<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cyprus Convention</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1878">1878</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> Convention was a secret agreement signed on 4 June 1878 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. Britain undertook to defend the Ottoman lands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, and in return the sultan allowed it to occupy and administer Cyprus while keeping formal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>. Britain annexed the island outright in 1914 when the Ottomans entered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s side.</p></div>
